# PROVEN FALSE MEMBERS of the per-family noreturn census (tools/gen_noreturn_syms.py).
# The governing principle: a name-keyed, build-wired FAMILY census cannot be right for
# every caller at once, because "does this callee return" is PER-TU knowledge. Two
# measured admission classes express that:
#
#   CLASS 1 (BOTH-WAYS CONFLICT, the original and still the common one). Retail reaches
#   the symbol `j` from a tail call AND `jal` from a caller that uses the result
#   (tools/noreturn_census_guard.py REPORT 1). Membership is right for one caller and
#   wrong for the other.
#
#   CLASS 2 (WRONG-PASS OWNERSHIP, added 2026-09-01, func_80024948). Retail reaches the
#   symbol by `j` only -- so it is a legitimate LEAD 22 arg-sibcall dispatcher -- but a
#   noreturn DECLARATION somewhere in the family's scan set hands it to LEAD 18 instead.
#   The two passes are not interchangeable: LEAD 18 flips the opcode and nothing else,
#   while LEAD 22 SHAPE B/C also DELETES the dead `j $Lepilogue` + delay slot. On a
#   SHAPE B/C site LEAD 18's rewrite is therefore TWO WORDS long, and because LEAD 18
#   runs FIRST the site is no longer a `jal` for LEAD 22 to fix -- so the sibcall census
#   cannot repair it and the noreturn membership must go. Watch for a declaration that
#   comes from an UNLANDED work/overlay_wave/candidates_<fam>/ scratch file: candidates
#   self-serve their own decls at compile time (tools/overlay_evidence.py
#   evidence_env_with_candidate; the per-segment merge in
#   overlay_local_gate.compile_c_segments) and never needed tracked-census membership.
#   tools/gen_sibcall_syms.py's rule-3 neutrality audit fails closed on this class.
#
#   CLASS 3 (STALE CENSUS ENTRY, added 2026-09-22, the round-51/52 cohort). The symbol is an
#   ORDINARY RETURNING, usually argument-taking function: its definition returns a value or
#   falls through, and its caller consumes the result or keeps executing. The census entry
#   exists only because a stale zero-arg `noreturn` declaration for the name survives in the
#   frozen raw/ corpus the census is scanned from, and membership turns that caller's retail
#   `jal` into a `j`. These nine were reviewed per symbol and deleted BY HAND from
#   config/noreturn_syms.dungeon.txt in commits 337f02aa and 2179b161 with no record here, so
#   the census could not be regenerated at all; the records restore that. Each proof cites its
#   review document and the measurement in it.
#
# Excluding a symbol drops the family-wide maspsx LEAD 18 jal->j rewrite while every TU
# KEEPS its own `noreturn` attribute, so the declaring TU still gets its tail `j` from
# GCC (and, in a gate/compare, from the per-segment self-serve merge).
# `proof` is REQUIRED and must name the measurement, not an argument.
